e pre-commit checks.\n\n**Verdict** (`b57e9070`, trailer `WI: WI-881`, file `docs/reviews/wi-881/004-ADJUDICATE-0020593.md`, ending `SITTING: JUDGED kinds=amendment;first-approval`)\n\nAll three findings from sitting 001 are answered:\n- **Scope:** the guarantee now covers every process still in the session's process group (POSIX) or job (Windows). What falls outside is written into SR-238's Rationale.\n- **Timing:** the kill reaps the direct child, then waits until the group or job is empty, up to 10 s. On Windows it first stops new processes joining the job, takes a handle on each member, then terminates the job. That closes the short gap where the job reads empty before a terminated process has finished.\n- **Coverage:** interruption, refusing a child that can't be contained, a process created during the kill, and a member the kill can't open each have a real-process test.\n\nI checked that an error after the 10 s bound actually stops the coordinator; nothing on the way up catches it. `tests/test_session_stdin.py` gave 29 passed, no skips, on this Windows box.\n\n**Amendment: `VERDICT: MEANING rows=2`:**\n- **LLR-026: blessed.** Every clause matches `_kill_tree` and its helpers, in the stated order.\n- **TC-026: not blessed.** The new Expected text is right for SR-238, but it dropped SR-026's outcome. The old cell said \"Satisfies SR-026 AcceptanceCriteria\"; the new one lists only the kill conditions. TC-026 still claims to verify SR-026, and its Method still runs those cases, but nothing now says what they must show. That was probably accidental.\n\n**First approval: `OUTCOME: APPROVE rows=1`.** SR-238's guarantee now covers only processes the mechanism can reach, its 10 s line can be observed, and its chain covers every acceptance arm. One observation, not a finding: the error after 10 s names the surviving group or the job's process count, not individual Windows process IDs. Listing them would make an operator's next step quicker.\n\n**Acts:**\n- **Re-attesta